\par\par \b \uc2 RBNZ seeks power to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  market.  \b0\par\par\uc2 333 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 21:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, March 11 (Reuters) - The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday it wanted the power to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to influence the level of the New Zealand dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank's current stance is to use its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  only if the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market became "disorderly" but it has not done so since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was floated in early 1985.  \par \par \uc2 Reserve Bank Governor Alan Bollard said in a statement accompanying the bank's monetary policy statement that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would recommend to the government that it be given the ability to use New Zealand dollars to buy \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , putting downward pressure on the exchange rate.  \par \par \uc2 "And, when the exchange rate is exceptionally and unjustifiably low, we would be able to sell \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy New Zealand dollars, putting upwards pressure on the exchange rate," he said.  \par \par \uc2 "By unjustifiable, we mean when the exchange rate has moved to a level in excess of that readily explained by the relevant economic fundamentals, which occurs only infrequently," Bollard said.  \par \par \uc2 Bollard said the process proposed is similar to that used by the Reserve Bank of Australia for some years.  \par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar has been one of the strongest performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past year rising around 25 percent against the U.S. dollar. The RBNZ said the kiwi was around 15 percent above its long-term average on a trade weighted basis .  \par \par \uc2 He said the general aim would be to influence the exchange rate in a way consistent with maintaining price stability and that the bank would not seek to change the long-run exchange rate.  \par \par \uc2 "At best, we can influence the exchange rate only by a small amounts at the extremes of its cycle when it is a long way from economic fundamentals," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Bollard said more work and consultation was needed before final decisions could be made and procedures put in place.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040311e03a000ub\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
