\par\par \b \uc2 NZD Down As Fin Min Says May  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Just Down  \b0\par\par\uc2 720 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 2004\par 06:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar closed sharply lower against the U.S. dollar Friday after the finance minister hinted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might soon \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise, for the first time in nearly 20 years.  \par \par \uc2 New Zealand government bond prices closed just a touch lower as a slight overhang of supply and weak sentiment sent the local market in the opposite direction to overseas bonds.  \par \par \uc2 Yields closed on their intraday highs as the market took on an offered tone after the Kiwi - as the New Zealand Dollar is colloquially known - sank.  \par \par \uc2 After trading in a local range of US$0.6977 to US$0.7021, the New Zealand dollar closed at US$0.6977, down from Thursday's close of US$0.7016.  \par \par \uc2 Against the Australian dollar, the Kiwi, as the local unit is known, closed at A$0.8844, down from Thursday's close at A$0.8862.  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Michael Cullen said the Reserve Bank of New Zealand is concerned about the relatively low level of its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves by international standards.  \par \par \uc2 "The Reserve Bank of New Zealand wants to build up its reserves, and it's reported to me along those lines," Cullen told Dow Jones Newswires.  \par \par \uc2 "(A)t the same time the bank and Treasury are finalizing advice on options for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added, noting that a report is due from the Treasury in three to four weeks.  \par \par \uc2 To build up its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the RBNZ would have to buy them with New Zealand dollars. The local unit is expected to be pushed lower by the Kiwi selling or by sentiment from that selling.  \par \par \uc2 The Kiwi was little changed overnight and was supported by "reasonably good buying across the board" during the local session, said Basil Payn, Westpac head of spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "Obviously those comments from Dr. Cullen knocked it down from US$0.7035 to US$0.6995," said Payn about 40 minutes before the local close.  \par \par \uc2 Payn said the comments likely had more effect on offshore investors, as local investors were used to such jawboning against the Kiwi's strength. "There may be some lightening up of long positions."  \par \par \uc2 Sue Trinh, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of New Zealand, said it was unclear if Cullen's words would carry any longer-term repercussions on the market.  \par \par \uc2 "As it is, the local market's remaining rather skeptical that the RBNZ will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," she said.  \par \par \uc2 Trinh picked an overnight range of US$0.6950 to US$7010 while Payn predicted the Kiwi to trade between US$0.6960 and US$0.7050 overnight.  \par \par \uc2 Payn also noted that just after Cullen made his comments, Dallas U.S Federal Reserve head Robert McTeer was quoted saying he wasn't "going to cry about the dollar against the euro," which is likely to prompt a further bout of U.S. dollar weakness.  \par \par \uc2 "You may see Kiwi/U.S. a little bit stronger over the weekend, but we may be weaker against some of the crosses."  \par \par \uc2 After opening steady bond yields closed up half a basis point in the short bonds and up 1.5 basis points in the long bonds.  \par \par \uc2 "The local market felt heavy and there was a lack of buyers," said one bond trader. "After Cullen's comments the short end took on an offered tone," having had a bid tone earlier.  \par \par \uc2 There was also paying interest in the two-year and four-year swaps, an investment bank trader said. Traders said there was interest to pay fixed from bank mortgage books.  \par \par \uc2 The bond curve steepened, with the gap between the 6.5% February 2006 and the 6.5% April 2013 closing at 37.5 basis points from 36.5 basis points Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 6.5% February '2006:       5.520% vs 5.515% \par 6.5% April '13:            5.895% vs 5.880% \par 90-day Bank Bill:          5.59%  vs  5.56% \par 10-Yr Spread To U.S.:      +185 bps vs +183 bps \par 10-Yr Spread To Australia: +32 bps vs +30 bps \par Mar 04 Bank Bill Future:   94.40  vs 94.40 \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By John Barton & Christopher Niesche, Dow Jones Newswires; 644 4715990; john.barton@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1062 20710 4171  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040220e02k0005j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
