\par\par \b \uc2 Fin Min: RBNZ, Tsy Finalizing Advice On  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Benjamin Pedley  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 839 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 2004\par 03:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Finance Minister Michael Cullen Friday gave his clearest indication that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might soon \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for the first time in almost 20 years.  \par \par \uc2 The government is concerned that strength in the local unit, which is up almost 70% against the U.S. dollar over the past two years, will damp exports and the overall economy.  \par \par \uc2 Cullen said the Reserve Bank of New Zealand is concerned about the relatively low level of its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves by international standards.  \par \par \uc2 "The Reserve Bank of New Zealand wants to build up its reserves, and its reported to me along those lines," said Cullen. "Its levels of reserves haven't changed since 1990, and I'm getting a final report back in three to four weeks time, and at the same time the bank and Treasury are finalizing advice on options for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said in an interview with Dow Jones Newswires.  \par \par \uc2 At 0220 GMT, the New Zealand dollar was at US$0.7010, down from US$0.7035 just prior to Cullen's remarks.  \par \par \uc2 Cullen said that if the policy of nonintervention changes then the Reserve Bank of New Zealand's approach would be similar to that of its Australian counterpart.  \par \par \uc2 "The RBA has two different approaches, one is what it calls replenishing its reserves, and the second is where they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . I think it would be sensible that the Reserve Bank of New Zealand would operate in a similar fashion," he said, speaking on the phone from his office in Wellington, New Zealand.  \par \par \uc2 It seems, however, more a question of when rather than if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shifts its approach.  \par \par \uc2 When asked whether \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely in the coming months or this year, the minister said: "I wouldn't rest easy on the assumption that the settings for the last 20 years are going to remain unchanged, I would be inclined to factor that in to one's judgment."  \par \par \uc2 The finance minister said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  independently has been "concerned about the level of reserves being adequate to deal with market disruption."  \par \par \uc2 "We've been working for some time on that and we have come to the conclusion that by international standards our reserves are rather lower than would be expected," he said, referring to discussions with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank's current \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve target is a range of 1.4 billion to 1.7 billion special drawing rights, a notional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  used by the International Monetary Fund. Actual reserves stand around 1.5 billion SDRs, which equates to NZ$3.6 billion.  \par \par \uc2 How the reserves are increased is crucial, said Cullen, adding that they could be upped either by borrowing offshore, or borrowing onshore and purchasing foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "What it would mean is one significant break in policy, which has been government policy for a considerable number of years, which is maintaining net zero foreign exposure," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Despite the possible shift in policy, Cullen emphasized that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't a cure-all.  \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can only have a limited effect in topping off the extremes in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , you can't affect the cycle itself or the direction of change, so even if the RBNZ had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we would have still seen a large appreciation in the Kiwi against the U.S. dollar over the past year," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The New Zealand \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is colloquially referred to as the Kiwi after the nation's flightless bird.  \par \par \uc2 Turning to the outlook for the economy, Cullen said exchange rates will be the major influence on forecasts for gross domestic product growth in coming years.  \par \par \uc2 "Most advisers would suspect that growth is continuing to run faster than forecast....but I think people are starting to think now that the dollar will have an impact on slowing the economy quicker toward the end of this year and running into 2005," he said.  \par \par \uc2 An Economic & Fiscal Update issued December forecast GDP growth of 2.8% for the year ending March 2005 - unchanged from a very conservative projection of growth through March 2004 - accelerating to 3.4% in 2005/06.  \par \par \uc2 When asked about possible revisions to the forecast for 2004/05 in the government budget to be issued May 27, he indicated it would be unchanged.  \par \par \uc2 "I think there are over and unders which are likely to even out on the 2.8% figure, (which) would be the best guess. Looking beyond that, it is going to depend on when the U.S. dollar starts to turn, or the New Zealand dollar starts to turn on its own," he said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Benjamin Pedley, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4044; ben.pedley@dowjones.com \par    (Benjamin Pedley, chief Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  correspondent for Dow Jones Newswires, has covered the market for seven years and appears daily on CNBC Asia. Previously he traded \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for institutions in Sydney and Hong Kong.)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Simon Harvey  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040220e02k0001w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
