\par\par \b \uc2 NZ WATCH: Fin Min May Be Serious About NZD  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 1,126 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Februar 2004\par 02:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Stephen Wright \par    A Dow Jones Newswires Column \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--Markets like to dismiss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 New Zealand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Finance Minister Michael Cullen's hints about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market as mere saber rattling. But his track record of fiddling with policy frameworks - and his skepticism of pure free market policies - suggest he's determined to act in some way.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Cullen's latest outburst about the skyrocketing New Zealand dollar - which is now at seven-year highs around US$0.70 - was notable in that he broke with his previous refusal to provide specifics and gave some detail about his options for influencing the New Zealand dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "Increasing \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves may have an impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate," he told Parliament's finance and expenditure select committee Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Cullen went on to say that he hasn't yet decided if he will instruct the Reserve Bank of New Zealand to increase its reserves. "I'm still discussing that with the Reserve Bank."  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank's current \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve target is a range of 1.4 billion to 1.7 billion special drawing rights, a notional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  used by the International Monetary Fund. Actual reserves stand around 1.5 billion SDRs, which equates to NZ$3.6 billion.  \par \par \uc2 Cullen's comments suggest his talks with Treasury and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials, first revealed late last year, have progressed significantly. His comments - which were most spooky for offshore players less familiar with the local scene - helped drag the New Zealand dollar down about 30 points Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 One reason to dismiss Cullen's remarks as posturing is a broad-based local consensus that direct \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have a minimal effect at best. Japan's heroic and expensive effort to block the yen's rise is frequently cited as an example of the futility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's quick recovery from Wednesday's jawboning is seen as a perfect illustration that fundamental trends in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't be defeated.  \par \par \uc2 "The overnight price action proved that this thing is a lot bigger than the finance minister. USD sentiment is what it's all about right now, and thus Greenspan's testimony revived the NZD," said Bank of New Zealand \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Sue Trinh in a note Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciated 25% against the U.S. dollar in 2003 and 26% in the previous year. So far this year, the New Zealand dollar has already appreciated by 6.4%.  \par \par \uc2 In the early stages of that appreciation, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was recovering from a clearly undervalued level - it hit a post-1985 float low of US$0.3898 in October 2000. But more recently, general U.S. dollar weakness has driven the Kiwi's ascent, resulting in it overshooting into overvalued territory according to some economic models.  \par \par \uc2 Another popular reason to dismiss Cullen is politics. The strength of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  means the New Zealand economy risks a hard landing in 2005 - an election year - so it is in the government's interests to be perceived by voters as addressing the problem, even if it does nothing substantial.  \par \par \uc2 In some quarters, personal annoyance with the often prickly finance minister may play a part. One senior dealer said he wouldn't comment on the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as he didn't want to give Cullen the satisfaction of thinking he was being taken seriously.  \par \par \uc2 But Cullen, with his attacks on the Reserve Bank in the lead-up to 2002 general election, and his subsequent changes to the Policy Targets Agreement, which made for more flexible monetary policy, has shown he's not afraid to buck convention or disregard what markets think.  \par \par \uc2 In fact, with a whole range of other policy initiatives and decisions, Cullen and the Labour-led administration have shown a tendency to want to modify the free market orthodoxy that has prevailed in New Zealand since the mid-1980s.  \par \par \uc2 For example, in 2001 the government used taxpayer funds for a massive - by local standards - bailout of Air New Zealand (though it stopped short of renationalizing the carrier).  \par \par \uc2 With last year's reforms to the electricity market - which, due to New Zealand's dependence on hydroelectricity, periodically suffers supply shortages and massive price spikes - Cullen was instrumental in adding a layer of regulation and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the industry, though he left free market fundamentals intact.  \par \par \uc2 Thus it would be entirely consistent for Cullen to steer clear of radical steps like capital controls or abandoning the floating exchange rate, but to direct the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to increase its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves with the aim of slowing the New Zealand dollar's rise. Cullen might hope that such action would be the catalyst for a correction lower as soon as the current trend in global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets had run its course.  \par \par \uc2 Certainly the Reserve Bank has the expertise in money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sterilize any extra liquidity generated in the process of selling New Zealand dollars to buy the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Cullen's public comments about raising foreign reserves suggest he wouldn't hesitate to use direct and public methods in any effort to prevent \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar appreciation.  \par \par \uc2 However, covert, unpublicized market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through local banks wouldn't be inconceivable. The Reserve Bank might also try to exert moral pressure by calling the dealing rooms of local price-making banks to discuss their positions, or by leaving offers at a certain level - anything to convince the market that New Zealand dollar appreciation was no longer an entirely safe bet.  \par \par \uc2 One market observer points out that Cullen is putting billions of dollars into an investment fund to help pay for part of the cost of universal pensions - so if he's prepared to bet on equity markets, he might not blanche at throwing a couple of billion at the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 And although Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the yen is cited by some as a failure, it's viewed by others as a success - the yen has appreciated much less steeply against the dollar than other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have in the past couple of years, and this has helped protect Japanese exports.  \par \par \uc2 Most market participants remain reluctant to accept that \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  will break with its clean float and experiment with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - it's not known to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  once since the float.  \par \par \uc2 But the idea of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  trying to influence the New Zealand dollar isn't laughed off by dealers quite as quickly as it was just a few weeks ago - and that in itself is a significant shift in market sentiment.  \par \par \uc2 -By Stephen Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 64-4-471-5990; stephen.wright@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Andrew Torchia  \par \par \uc2 1138 20713 4190  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040212e02c00028\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
