\par\par \b \uc2 NZ govt eyes options on kiwi dlr - PM Clark.  \b0\par\par\uc2 320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Januar 2004\par 01:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, Jan 16 (Reuters) - New Zealand Prime Minister Helen Clark reiterated on Friday there was little the government could do to stem the kiwi dollar's rise, but it was mulling with Treasury whether there were options "on the margins".  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in November it was reviewing the tools it could use to influence the resurgent kiwi dollar in the wake of comments from Finance Minister Michael Cullen that he had unspecified options to curb the kiwi's climb.  \par \par \uc2 The government is concerned at the impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sharp rise on the exporters. The New Zealand dollar , one of the top performing developed \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2003, scaled fresh six-and-a-half year highs this week, peaking at around 68.7 U.S. cents.  \par \par \uc2 "I think most people accept that our dollar's been driven up because of the U.S. dollar's weakness and no-one expects the government to perform a minor miracle over that," Clark told Radio New Zealand. "He (Cullen) and Treasury will obviously be looking at whether there's anything that one can do on the margins and he's the best person to talk to about that."  \par \par \uc2 "But when the U.S. dollar's in a dive everyone else is affected."  \par \par \uc2 Clark acknowledged exporters, particularly farmers battling dry weather conditions on the east coast of the South Island, were feeling the pain of the kiwi's 25 percent gain against the greenback last year.  \par \par \uc2 "I think it's the rate of change, the volatility, that most affects exporters," she said.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has never \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since the kiwi dollar was freely floated in 1985, but has always reserved the right to do so.  \par \par \uc2 RBNZ Governor Alan Bollard said last year the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only consider \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if finance markets were severely disrupted.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040116e01g00030\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
