\par\par \b \uc2 NZ WATCH: Fin Min Doesn't Like His Kiwi Overcooked  \b0\par\par\uc2 782 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 2003\par 05:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Stephen Wright \par  \par    A Dow Jones Newswires Column \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--Finance Minister Michael Cullen's hint he could curb the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 New Zealand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar's strength through \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market has been greeted with skepticism, if not outright derision.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 "Saddam Hussein led the world to believe he had weapons of mass destruction...and Michael Cullen is trying to let the markets know he has weapons of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  suppression," said Tony Alexander, an economist at Bank of New Zealand, in a response that underlined the lack of credibility given to Cullen's remarks.  \par \par \uc2 The finance minister sparked a minor media sensation on Wednesday this week - but failed to move the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  one iota - with his response to a question on what he will do about the high New Zealand dollar, which is causing pain for exporters.  \par \par \uc2 "The government doesn't regard itself as entirely without options in this respect," he told Parliament's finance and expenditure select committee.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of New Zealand Act enables the country's Treasurer - currently Cullen - to direct the monetary authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and also requires the bank to hold \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves for that purpose.  \par \par \uc2 But the Reserve Bank hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was floated in 1985.  \par \par \uc2 Cullen was next asked if he would use his "options" for dealing with the kiwi - a shy, flightless and near extinct native bird that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is named for.  \par \par \uc2 "That's a matter I would prefer not to comment on at this point," he told the committee. "I'm always considering doing all sorts of things. Whether I'm considering doing something in that area is for me to know."  \par \par \uc2 He was even less illuminating on the subject when asked in parliament the next day if he was signaling changes to the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Act, changes to the floating exchange rate, or \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 "My intention was to signal that the government isn't without options. No specific conclusions can be drawn from that statement and it would be most unwise to do so," Cullen said.  \par \par \uc2 His most obvious options for attempting to influence the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has risen about 50% against the U.S. dollar since the beginning of last year, seem to be either directing the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell the kiwi, or imposing some form of controls on the flow of capital.  \par \par \uc2 But the first option would have at best a temporary impact as the New Zealand dollar is in an upward trend against the U.S. dollar and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't defeat this trend, which is driven by economic fundamentals, said Westpac \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Johnathan Bayley.  \par \par \uc2 If Japan's monetary authorities, which have accumulated years of experience at \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , can't halt the rise of the yen against the U.S. dollar then New Zealand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't have any luck at stopping the Kiwi's rise against the dollar, he added.  \par \par \uc2 Another factor making \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near to medium-term implausible is the fact the Reserve Bank of New Zealand is expected to raise interest rates in the first quarter of next year.  \par \par \uc2 It would look rather "incongruous" for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try and weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  while at the same supporting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with higher official interest rate, said Deutsche Bank Economist Darren Gibbs.  \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  normally does not work unless the market is about ready to move there anyway...when things are absolutely extended and the market is looking for a catalyst to turn, that is the time to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 With the Kiwi sitting around US$0.61 and potentially going much higher "you would be asking for trouble if you \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Gibbs. "Hedge funds around the world would go 'great, money to be made in New Zealand'."  \par \par \uc2 However, Cullen may also have had in mind steps like a capital gains tax to take the heat out the country's housing market, said Gibbs. Such a tax could weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the impact was interest rates not rising, or not rising as much as they would otherwise.  \par \par \uc2 The second major option - of imposing capital controls - seems an unthinkable, backward step in an open, deregulated economy like New Zealand.  \par \par \uc2 "Cullen is playing to a domestic audience with his comments...and I don't think he for one minute he seriously contemplates" capital controls, said Bank of New Zealand's Alexander.  \par \par \uc2 -By Stephen Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 64-4-471-5990; stephen.wright@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Costas Paris  \par \par \uc2 1138 20713 4190  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031107dzb70004i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
