\par\par \b \uc2 Fin Min Asks Agencies For NZD  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Ideas - Report  \b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 2003\par 21:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Finance Minister Michael Cullen has asked the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Treasury Department to report on ways to curb the rising New Zealand dollar, the Dominion Post newspaper reported Thursday without citing its source.  \par \par \uc2 The newspaper said it understands that Cullen is exploring how the two government agencies could use existing activities such as the issuing and timing of government bonds or \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading to influence the New Zealand dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The report follows comments by Cullen to Parliament's finance and expenditure select committee Wednesday in which he hinted at the possibility of the government ordering \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Asked in the committee what he will do about the high New Zealand dollar, Cullen said "the government doesn't regard itself as entirely without options in this respect."  \par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar has gained about 50% against the U.S. dollar since the beginning of last year, denting export returns.  \par \par \uc2 The Dominion Post report quoted opposition National Party deputy finance spokesman John Key urging caution.  \par \par \uc2 "While there is concern about the impact that a rising exchange rate is having on our exporters, Dr. Cullen's options are very limited," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Key said the last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in the mid-1990s when the Reserve Bank sold about NZ$200 million to smooth the exchange rate. It had "shock effect" but little long-term impact.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of New Zealand, in a report on its Web site, said it maintains \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves so that it has the capability to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  but hasn't done so since the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was floated in 1985.  \par \par \uc2 -Wellington Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; 64-4-471-5990; djnews.wellington@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020031105dzb5000ye\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
