\par\par \b \uc2  NZ dollar ends above key support, bonds firm. \b0\par\par\uc2 469 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2002\par 07:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  AUCKLAND, Dec 5 (Reuters) - The New Zealand dollar ended above key support on Thursday as the market awaited the outcome of the Auckland City Council's decision on the possible sale of its one quarter stake in Auckland International Airport (AIA.NZ). \par \par \uc2  A decision to proceed with the sale, worth around NZ$400 million ($200 million) at current market prices, was likely to lend some support for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  while a decision against could lead to a fall. \par \par \uc2  A dip below $0.5000 was seen as possible if the council decided against it or a rally over $0.5050 if it was approved, based on the possibility of NZ$400 million washing through the market. \par \par \uc2  But the focus generally was on the U.S. dollar versus the yen, particularly in light of Japan's weak yen policy. \par \par \uc2  "People seem to be taking on board the Bank of Japan's comments and getting short yen and long everything else," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  Another key issue for the market was whether the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  opts to cut rates by the 50 basis points the market expects when it meets later on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  New Zealand Finance Minister Michael Cullen's comments that the kiwi was at the top end of its "comfort zone" against the Australian dollar, but not overpriced against the U.S. dollar, stopped the kiwi's rally in its tracks at around $0.5030. \par \par \uc2  Cullen said New Zealand manufacturing exporters would be more comfortable if the kiwi  cross rate against the Aussie retreated at least five percent from near five-year highs around 89.5 Australian cents. \par \par \uc2  "It (NZD) still is very much at the top end of the comfort zone on the Australian cross rate," Cullen told Reuters in an interview. \par \par \uc2  But with \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy of non-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its exchange rate, Cullen's comments were largely dismissed as talk. \par \par \uc2  "It was a bit of a nothing comment at the end of the day," said one dealer. \par \par \uc2  "I guess there was some initial reaction to it but the market was actually struggling above the $0.5030 level when it came out anyway. There was limited topside at that point in time," he said. \par \par \uc2  The kiwi finished at $0.5013/23, up from Wednesday's close of $0.4985/95, and above key support at $0.5005. \par \par \uc2  In the corporate bond market, Transpower's 2006 bond issue went off at an eight basis point premium to the equivalent swap. In governments, the local yield curve ended flatter. \par \par \uc2  February 2005 bonds were unchanged at 5.79 percent while the November 2006s dropped a basis point to 5.95 percent. \par \par \uc2  July 2009 bonds ended at 6.22 percent, down two, and the April 2013s at 6.33 percent, down four. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021205dyc500ccj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
