\par\par \b \uc2  NZ Dollar Down Early; Tracks A$, Euro; OCR Review Wed \b0\par\par\uc2 487 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juni 2002\par 23:33\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WELLINGTON -(Dow Jones)- The New Zealand dollar was slightly lower against the U.S. dollar early Monday in Wellington as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tracked its Australian counterpart offshore and held within recent ranges. \par \par \uc2  At 2123 GMT, the New Zealand dollar was quoted at US$0.4872, down from US$0.4878 late Friday in Wellington. \par \par \uc2  A Wellington bank dealer said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  initially tracked the Australian dollar higher offshore and slipped after the euro weakened following \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Japan and Federal Reserve. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar traded a US$0.4852 and US$0.4912 range overnight, and dealers expect a similar range during the Asian session Monday. \par \par \uc2  The previous week was marked by some volatile trading as  investors reacted to news out of the U.S., with the WorldCom Inc. scandal dominating markets and sentiment for several days. \par \par \uc2  The US$.3.8 billion WorldCom fraud drove investors toward safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which hurt the Australian and New Zealand dollars. However, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  managed to hold out the US$0.4850 support after breaking those levels once last week. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say the New Zealand dollar is likely to range-trade between the US$0.4800 and US$0.5000 region as offshore investors continue to rejigger their U.S. dollar positions amid forecasts of further depreciation for the greenback. \par \par \uc2  A second dealer said the Xerox blowup has yet again highlighted the problems wracking U.S. corporates. The office equipment concern said Friday it expects to restate revenues by about US$2 billion over a five-year period. \par \par \uc2  "The corporate news out of the U.S. just keeps getting  worse, and there are still concerns about the pace of U.S. economic growth," he said. "All this will keep the Kiwi on  the backfoot with  investors on a cautious footing." \par \par \uc2  He said factors which had driven the New Zealand dollar - interest rate differentials and a robust economy - will continue to underpin support for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the medium term. \par \par \uc2  Johnathan Bayley, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Westpac Bank, said the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will remain a "laggard" in the dollar-bloc due to the cautious tone in international markets. \par \par \uc2  Key technical support is seen at US$0.4780, a 50% retracement on a line between the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's May 1999 high and its all-time low, at US0.3898, recorded in October 2000. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to raise the official cash rate by 25 basis points to 5.75%, the fourth 25-basis-point upward adjustment to short-term rates since mid-March, in order to protect its zero-to-3% annual inflation target. \par \par \uc2  Against the Australian dollar, the New Zealand dollar was quoted at A$0.8643, up a little from A$0.8640 late Friday in Wellington. \par \par \uc2  -By Shri Navaratnam, Dow Jones Newswires; 644 4715990; shri.navaratnam@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1062 20711 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020630dy6u000h9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
