\par\par \b \uc2  New Zealand's Nonintervention In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Market Served Econ Well-Report \b0\par\par\uc2 275 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 April 2002\par 07:09\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WELLINGTON -(Dow Jones)- The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's long-standing policy of not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has served the economy well, according to a research report published in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's quarterly Bulletin Friday. \par \par \uc2  "Inflation targeting and a policy of nonintervention in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets have so far proved effective in maintaining price stability and avoiding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crises," the report said. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank has since the late 1980s directed monetary policy with an aim to maintaining stability in the general level of prices. The New Zealand dollar became a free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1985. \par \par \uc2  This dual approach has provided appropriate incentives to the private sector to hedge their foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be "happy" with its approach, the report said. \par \par \uc2  The report was written by Nils Bjorksten and Anne-Marie Brook, analysts at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Economics Department. \par \par \uc2  The authors also said, however, that there is a developing view among international academics that free-floating exchange rates don't deliver as many benefits as some had anticipated in the 1980s. \par \par \uc2  The report also examines the potential benefits and drawbacks of New Zealand abandoning its independently floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in favor of either joining a larger monetary union or alternatively adopting the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The full report can be viewed at the following Web site: \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.rbnz.govt.nz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.rbnz.govt.nz}}}\par \par \uc2  -By Chris Ritchie, Dow Jones Newswires; 644 4715990; chris.ritchie@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (This story was originally published by Dow Jones Newswires) \par \par \uc2  Copyright (c) 2002 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2  All Rights Reserved \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020405dy45000a7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
