\par\par \b \uc2  NZ Dlr Down Slightly In Late Trade; Looks To Offshore Mkts \b0\par\par\uc2 567 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 2000\par 06:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WELLINGTON -(Dow Jones)- The New Zealand dollar is slightly weaker versus the U.S. dollar in local afternoon trade Monday after trading quietly in a very narrow range. \par \par \uc2  Around 0500 GMT the New Zealand dollar is quoted at US$0.3995, down from US$0.4001 late Friday in Wellington, and just higher than its local open at US$0.3993. \par \par \uc2  The New Zealand \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has traded in a range of US$0.3992 to US$0.3997 Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers noted the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro twice Friday, however the effort largely failed to provide much of a boost. They said the New Zealand and Australian dollars continue to be guided by the euro direction, but the same dealers were mixed on their outlook for the European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  One technical analyst said the euro appears to have reached a turning point, and further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could push it substantially higher. \par \par \uc2  He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar has been very quiet Monday. \par \par \uc2  "Probably the focus is on the U.S. (presidential) election upcoming midweek. The central banks \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  (to support the euro) Friday night but that had a pretty muted effect," he said. \par \par \uc2  "But I wouldn't count them out of things. I wouldn't be surprised if we see another significant burst of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and this time I think it's going to work - the charts are suggesting the euro is in some sort of turning phase at the moment," he said. \par \par \uc2  The analyst said the euro could easily push up towards US$0.9500-US$0.9700 in the next month or two, which would encourage the New Zealand dollar up towards the US$0.4300 level. \par \par \uc2  A bank dealer said both the New Zealand and Australian dollar markets have been very quiet. He also noted a general recovery in "dollar/regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  - which includes the Thai baht, the Taiwan dollar, the Philippine peso," he said. \par \par \uc2  "So I think that bodes well for support in kiwi and aussie - but that's not to say they can't trade lower," he added. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said he is picking the euro to weaken versus the U.S. dollar following a pullback from the post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  high. This could weigh on the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Australian dollars. \par \par \uc2  "I would buy (New Zealand dollar) dips at this stage but I would buy them quite deep," he said, adding it is possible the New Zealand \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will trade down to US$0.3900 or lower. \par \par \uc2  On a cross rate with the neighboring Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the local dollar is quoted at A$0.7586, down from A$0.7641 late Friday and higher than A$0.7581 early Monday. \par \par \uc2  On a cross rate with the Japanese yen, the local dollar was quoted at Y42.86, down from Y43.27 late Friday and higher than Y42.72 early Monday. \par \par \uc2  Against its trade weighted index, the New Zealand dollar is 46.59, down from 46.83 late Friday and higher than 46.52 early Monday. \par \par \uc2  Around 0330 GMT the Reserve Bank's Monetary Conditions Index, which is a composite measure of the trade-weighted index measure of the New Zealand dollar and yields on 90-day bank bills, was at minus-1053. \par \par \uc2  -By Alan Wood; Dow Jones Newswires; 64 4 801 8960; alan.wood@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1062 20711 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dwb605d6k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
