\par\par \b \uc2  NZ dollar creeps up after RBA, ECB  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 409 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 2000\par 22:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2   --------------------------------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2   * DAY'S RANGE * SUPPORT * RESTNCE * RSI-27 * MA-10  * MA-20 \par \par \uc2   * 0.3980-4020 * 0.3950  * 0.4025  * 27 PCT * 0.3980 * 0.3979 \par \par \uc2   ----------------VIEWS FROM THE MARKET (Nov 6)----------------- \par \par \uc2      * NZ dollar buoyed briefly by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in AUD, euro \par \par \uc2      * Price performance seen disappointing as flows still weigh \par \par \uc2      * Eyes on U.S. election for direction of USD policy. \par \par \uc2  WELLINGTON, Nov 6 (Reuters) - The New Zealand dollar was again hovering around $0.4000 in lacklustre early trading on Monday after receiving a brief boost from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Australian dollar and the euro overnight. \par \par \uc2  The kiwi climbed to a high of $0.4039 overnight on news both the Reserve Bank of Australia and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an effort to limit the slides in their respective \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  One dealer said the price movement of the kiwi was disappointing given the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It's a pretty dismal effort in the face of the RBA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the ECB - you'd have to say the price in the face of that's pretty dismal." \par \par \uc2  Natural flows were still weighted against the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in particular, he said. \par \par \uc2  ANZ Investment was also unimpressed with the brief rally in the kiwi. \par \par \uc2  "It is difficult to read too much into this move however, and the ease with which the kiwi (and the euro and AUD) has retraced sub-$0.4000 again is a concern," ANZ said in its Morning Brief commentary. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could lend some further support to the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar on the day. "I think (the kiwi) will be underlyingly bid because people might have got caught a little bit short from the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight. I think the risk is it might still rally a bit more from these levels," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The outcome of the U.S. presidential election would be the major short-term focus for the market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "I think we'll have to wait for the election over there to see what shape and form the new government takes and who's going to lead the Treasury and what sort of a dollar policy they adopt," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Markets were waiting to see if the administration would mean any significant changes for the rampant U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  "U.S. secretary Summers wants a strong dollar policy and until that changes, we going to see the (New Zealand) \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  struggle," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwb502lss\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
