\par\par \b \uc2  NZ Dlr Up Late On Euro  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Resistance US$0.415 \b0\par\par\uc2 374 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2000\par 08:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WELLINGTON -(Dow Jones)- The \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is up against the U.S. dollar in local trading late Monday, with dealers saying the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  benefited in the wake of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro after the local close Friday. \par \par \uc2  At 0545 GMT, the New Zealand dollar was trading at US$0.4115, up from US$0.4085 late Friday in Wellington but below its session high of US$0.4155, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Most of the day's trading was dull apart from an earlier surge up. We saw a gradual drift lower as the day progressed, with perhaps some importers taking some advantage from slightly better levels (in the New Zealand dollar) than they have seen recently," a bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  A second bank dealer said the local market is wary about further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro, adding that this can be expected to lend support for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on any dips toward US$0.4090 after the local close. \par \par \uc2  A third dealer said while the outlook for the New Zealand dollar has brightened thanks to the coordinated action to bolster the euro, it is important that the New Zealand dollar remains above US$0.4070 for this brighter outlook to remain valid. \par \par \uc2  Selling interest toward US$0.4150 is expected to offer initial resistance overnight. Further resistance is reported around US$0.4180, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  On a cross against the Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the New Zealand dollar is quoted at A$0.7552, up from A$0.7468 late Friday in Wellington. On a cross rate with the yen, the local dollar is quoted at Y44.36, up from Y43.67 late Friday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 2245 GMT Monday, or 10:45 a.m. Tuesday local time, Statistics New\par Zealand will publish its August overseas merchandise imports report. The\par median expectation of economists surveyed by Dow Jones Newswires is that\par imports were valued at NZ$2.54 billion in August, up 10% from NZ$2.31\par billion in the year-earlier month. In July, imports were 13% higher than\par in July 1999.\par -By Chris Ritchie, Dow Jones Newswires; 64 4-8018960; critchie@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1062 20711 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw9p04msa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
