\par\par \b \uc2  Cash rate best monetary tool currently in NZ-Brash. \b0\par\par\uc2 470 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2000\par 00:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WELLINGTON, May 9 (Reuters) - The governor of the Reserve Bank of New Zealand said on Tuesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's official cash rate (OCR) was the best monetary policy tool currently used. \par \par \uc2  However Brash told a media briefing on a government review of monetary policy \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it was worth reviewing the tool. \par \par \uc2  "Let's have an expert make a judgement," Brash said. \par \par \uc2  He pointed that the cash rate mechanism had only been introduced recently - in March last year. \par \par \uc2  It was worthwhile asking if this was a "sensible evolution" in monetary policy \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Brash said that international experience did not suggest that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was an effective method of determining a monetary policy stance. \par \par \uc2  This was also taken up by Finance Minister Michael Cullen, who is implementing the review. \par \par \uc2  Cullen said it would take an awful lot of convincing for him to back \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, Cullen announced that the monetary policy review will consider how the Reserve Bank of New Zealand (RBNZ) interprets and applies its inflation target and whether it has an adequate range of instruments to effectively manage monetary conditions. \par \par \uc2  He said the review will consider the following: \par \par \uc2  - The way the Reserve bank interprets and applies the inflation target set out in the Policy Targets Agreement with a view to ensuring that this approach to achieving medium term price stability is consistent with avoiding undesirable instability in output; \par \par \uc2  - Whether the Reserve Bank has an adequate range of instruments and is using its current instruments effectively in altering monetary conditions in the desired direction; \par \par \uc2  - The range of sources, availability, type and timeliness of data, and the impact of these variables on forecasting and decision making; \par \par \uc2  - Whether the policy decision making process and accountability structures promote the best outcomes possible; \par \par \uc2  - The co-ordination of monetary policy with other elements of the economic policy framework, including an evaluation of the relationship between monetary policy \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other Reserve Bank functions such as prudential oversight of financial institutions; \par \par \uc2  - Whether the Reserve Bank's communication of monetary policy decisions to the public and financial markets is as simple, clear and effective as possible. \par \par \uc2  Cullen said the total cost of the review, including the cost of using existing resources, is expected to be between NZ$200,000 and NZ$500,000. \par \par \uc2  It would be carried out by a reviewer from outside New Zealand, he said. \par \par \uc2  "Recommendations arising from the review will be discussed with the Reserve Bank Governor, Dr Don Brash, before the Government makes any decisions on how to proceed," Cullen said in speech notes for an address to a business audience in Wellington. \par \par \uc2  ((Wellington newsroom tel +64 4 471 4277, fax +64 4 473 6212 wellington.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw5800s8m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
