\par\par \b \uc2  NZ Dlr Up In Late Trading As Ctrl Bk Move Boosts Rates \b0\par\par\uc2 385 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Februar 1999\par 06:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--The New Zealand dollar surged to new nine month highs Monday on the Reserve Bank of New Zealand's surprise switch on monetary policy implementation which opened the way for higher interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Around 0440 GMT the New Zealand dollar is quoted at US$0.5588, up from US$0.5524 late Friday in Wellington, and up from its local open at US$0.5491. \par \par \uc2  The New Zealand dollar hasn't closed as high since April 27 last year. \par \par \uc2  It was a volatile session with the New Zealand \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a range of US$0.5482 to US$0.5588 Monday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the announcement the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had abandoned the monetary conditions index in favor of an official cash rate immediately underpinned the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as 90-day interest rates rose to 4.3%, from 4.08% late Friday. Traders said the expectation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will seek higher interest rates in March, when it sets the cash rate, pushed rates higher. They said it is expected that the cash rate will be set somewhat higher than prevailing 90-day rates. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it will continue to take account of the impact of the exchange rate on monetary policy as it has in the past, and argues that the new implementation policy will reduce volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. It said it hasn't changed its policy of not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Technical analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar could push toward US$0.5625, with support at US$0.5550. \par \par \uc2  Against its trade weighted index, the New Zealand dollar is 59.03, up from 58.25 late Friday and up from 58.14 early Monday. The TWI hasn't closed as high since June 1. \par \par \uc2  On a cross rate with the neighboring Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the local dollar is quoted at A$0.8562, up from A$0.8493 late Friday and up from A$0.8446 early Monday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On a cross rate with the yen, the local dollar was quoted at Y63.14,\par up from Y62.02 late Friday and up from Y62.15 early Monday.\par    -By Tracy Withers; 644 8018960\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 08-02-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0540GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1062 20711 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv280124o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
