\par\par \b \uc2  NZ Dollar Dn In Late Trading; But Supported By Yen Move \b0\par\par\uc2 355 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 1998\par 07:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--The New Zealand dollar is lower in local afternoon trade Friday, but has made gains from early local session weakness following strength in the yen versus the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Around 0510 GMT (1:10 a.m. EDT) the New Zealand dollar is quoted at US$0.5194, down from US$0.5203 late Thursday in Wellington, and higher than its local open at US$0.5167. \par \par \uc2  The New Zealand \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a range of US$0.5150 to US$0.5200 Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the New Zealand dollar Friday tracked moves in the yen versus the U.S. dollar and the local unit recovered from early weakness following a strengthening of the yen later in the session. \par \par \uc2  "The New Zealand dollar is closing with a bid tone, on the back of the yen strength opening up in the Tokyo afternoon session," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  "There hasn't been great volume on the day but there has been a couple of large sized buys," he said, adding the buyers were Singapore-based. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said with "Friday afternoon jitters", investors were squaring up their positions ahead of the weekend, particularly those with short positions. \par \par \uc2  One trader said early selling pressure on the New Zealand dollar has eased on the back of a strengthening yen. \par \par \uc2  "The market was caught a bit short and squeezed higher a couple of times. People at the moment just don't want to be caught too short in this market because of a fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the trader said. \par \par \uc2  "There's still talk of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . If the banks \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  you'll see the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar going to US$0.5300 pretty quickly," he added. \par \par \uc2  His comments follow a sharp rise in the yen early Thursday after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the U.S. Federal Reserve and the Bank of Japan to support the yen. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the New Zealand dollar will likely move in a range of US$0.5150 to US$0.5250 overnight. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 19-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0525GMT \par \par \uc2  1062 20711 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6j05ax2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
