\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Soars Vs Yen, Emerging Mkt  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Dn \b0\par\par\uc2  By Paul Podolsky \par \uc2 391 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 1998\par 22:26\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The dollar rallied further Monday, gaining almost 2 whole yen from its level late last week and also climbing against the Deutsche mark. \par \par \uc2  The yen's relentless slide lower is pummeling emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Southeast Asia, East Europe and Latin America. Investors are shifting assets en masse into the dollar, sterling and U.S. Treasurys. \par \par \uc2  The Indian rupee, South Korean won, Malaysian ringgit, Singapore dollar, South African rand and Mexican peso all fell against the dollar. The Russian ruble was flat following \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by that nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Australian and \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar also declined. \par \par \uc2  Late afternoon in New York, the dollar was trading at Y146.15, up from Y144.33 Friday in New York. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also trading at DEM1.8105, up from 1.8061 Friday. Sterling was trading at $1.6350, up from 1.6335. The dollar is at its highest level against the yen since August 1990. \par \par \uc2  "It's really more of the same," said Ricardo Gomes, managing director at Republic National Bank in New York. \par \par \uc2  Traders are selling the yen because Japan isn't attractive. Moreover, traders don't believe the U.S. Federal Reserve is prepared to jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the Bank of Japan to defend the yen unless Tokyo shepherds in fundamental reforms to open up Japanese markets and slash taxes. \par \par \uc2  In lieu of U.S. support, traders don't believe Japan alone poses a credible threat to more than temporarily reverse the yen's decline. Despite the Bank of Japan spending around $20 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  two months ago, traders note, the yen is still falling quickly. As a result, traders are increasingly ignoring Japanese leaders almost daily threats to take decisive action to boost the yen. \par \par \uc2  In the meantime, some believe pressure is increasingly mounting on China to devalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yuan, a step which traders believe could take other pegs with it, including the Hong Kong dollar, ruble and Brazilian real. \par \par \uc2  "The market is very nervous," said Gomes. This anxiety is reflected in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options where volatilities soared and market participants snapped up dollar/call yen/puts, or the right to buy dollars and sell yen. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 15-06-98 \par \par \uc2  2026GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 1865 20714 4164 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6f053q6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
