\par\par \b \uc2  NZ Dlr Up In Early Trade; Follows Australian Dlr Higher \b0\par\par\uc2 408 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 1998\par 23:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones Australia and New Zealand Report \par \uc2 DJAN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--The New Zealand dollar is higher in morning trade Tuesday, with dealers saying the local unit has tracked upwards on the back of a stronger Australian dollar. \par \par \uc2  Around 2055 GMT, the New Zealand dollar was quoted at US$0.4971, up from US$0.4955 late Monday in Wellington. \par \par \uc2  The New Zealand \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a range of US$0.4943 to US$0.4975 overnight. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the New Zealand dollar has found a regular trading range between US$0.4940 to US$0.5020, following a big fall in the value of the unit vs. the U.S. dollar last week. \par \par \uc2  "The kiwi dollar has opened a little better bid after reaching lows around US$0.4943 overnight," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market is waiting to see if there is any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Japanese yen vs. the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  "If there is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  it would probably give the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar a boost, but they could decide to stand aside and just let it go - so it's a bit of a waiting game at the moment," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  One dealer said both the Australian and New Zealand markets had been caught short of the respective \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the New Zealand dollar is following the Australian dollar higher. \par \par \uc2  He said once the Australian dollar stopped being squeezed higher, the New Zealand dollar was likely to move lower again. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the New Zealand dollar will likely move in a range of US$0.4945 to US$0.5000 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Against its trade weighted index, the New Zealand dollar rose to 56.85 from 56.78 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Around 2055 GMT the Reserve Bank's Monetary Conditions Index, which is a composite measure of the trade-weighted index measure of the NZ dollar and yields on 90-day bank bills, is at 244, or 106 basis points below the 350 level the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has outlined as appropriate on average during the third quarter of 1998. \par \par \uc2  On a cross rate with the neighboring Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the local dollar fell to A$0.8429 from A$0.8460 late Monday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On a cross rate with the Japanese yen, the local dollar rose to Y72.66\par from Y72.10 late Monday.\par    -By Alan Wood; 644-801-8960 awood@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 15-06-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2102GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1062 20711 \par \par \uc2 Dokument djan000020010916du6f001sl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
