\par\par \b \uc2  NZ Dlr Up In Early Trade; Follows Australian Dlr Higher \b0\par\par\uc2 408 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 1998\par 23:02\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--The New Zealand dollar is\par higher in morning trade Tuesday, with dealers saying the\par local unit has tracked upwards on the back of a stronger\par Australian dollar.\par    Around 2055 GMT, the New Zealand dollar was quoted at\par US$0.4971, up from US$0.4955 late Monday in Wellington.\par    The New Zealand \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traded in a range of\par US$0.4943 to US$0.4975 overnight.\par    Dealers said the New Zealand dollar has found a\par regular trading range between US$0.4940 to US$0.5020,\par following a big fall in the value of the unit vs. the\par U.S. dollar last week.\par    "The kiwi dollar has opened a little better bid after\par reaching lows around US$0.4943 overnight," one trader\par said.\par    Dealers said the market is waiting to see if there is\par any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the Japanese yen vs. the U.S.\par dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    "If there is \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  it would probably give the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 New Zealand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar a boost, but they could decide to stand\par aside and just let it go - so it's a bit of a waiting game\par at the moment," one trader said.\par    One dealer said both the Australian and New Zealand\par markets had been caught short of the respective\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and the New Zealand dollar is following the\par Australian dollar higher.\par    He said once the Australian dollar stopped being\par squeezed higher, the New Zealand dollar was likely to move\par lower again.\par    Traders said the New Zealand dollar will likely move\par in a range of US$0.4945 to US$0.5000 Tuesday.\par    Against its trade weighted index, the New Zealand\par dollar rose to 56.85 from 56.78 late Monday.\par    Around 2055 GMT the Reserve Bank's Monetary Conditions\par Index, which is a composite measure of the trade-weighted\par index measure of the NZ dollar and yields on 90-day bank\par bills, is at 244, or 106 basis points below the 350 level\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has outlined as appropriate on average\par during the third quarter of 1998.\par    On a cross rate with the neighboring Australian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the local dollar fell to A$0.8429 from A$0.8460\par late Monday.\par    On a cross rate with the Japanese yen, the local\par dollar rose to Y72.66 from Y72.10 late Monday.\par    -By Alan Wood; 644-801-8960 awood@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  06-15-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1702EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1062 20711 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du6f01gpy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
