\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Crisis At A Glance: Dlr Rises Past Y141, Then Retreats \b0\par\par\uc2 548 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 1998\par 13:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  -- The weakness in Japan's economic fundamentals is reflected in the current dollar-yen exchange rate, said Yasuo Goto, a member of the Bank of Japan's nine-member policy-making board. [R/JA] \par \par \uc2  -- There is a shared belief among G-7 officials that the excessively weak yen is negative for the global economy, Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Tanami said. [R/JA] \par \par \uc2  -- The dollar rose to a seven-year high above Y141 before receding on comments by LDP official Yamasaki, who urged the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  to make further efforts in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. At 0800 GMT, the dollar was at Y140.36, down from Y140.66 Monday in New York. [*R/JA] \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit, Thai baht, Philippine peso and Korean won rose on the yen's bounce against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  -- On broader yen weakness, Australasian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to weaken. The Australian dollar again fell below US$0.6000. The New Zealand dollar closed lower at $0.5064. \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Treasurer Peters said the government won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [*R/ASA] [*R/NZ] \par \par \uc2  -- The Hong Kong and Seoul stock indexes fell 2.1% and 1.9%, respectively, on yen weakness. [*R/HK][*R/SK] \par \par \uc2  -- Japan's Economic Planning Agency downgraded its assessment of three key components of the economy - housing construction, employment and imports - but cited signs of a recovery in consumption and left its overall view of the economy unchanged. \par \par \uc2  Japan's trade surplus will grow 9.3% in the fiscal year through March 1999 to Y14.88 trillion, while the current account surplus will rise 13.5% to Y14.80 trillion, a trade group said, according to the Nihon Keizai Shimbun. [*R/JA] \par \par \uc2  -- Bank Indonesia may cut interest rates and revise its year-end exchange rate target, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  director was quoted as saying, Bisnis Indonesia reported. The IMF is thought to be opposed to an interest rate cut. [*R/IO] \par \par \uc2  -- Hong Kong will maintain its iron link with the U.S. dollar and resist engaging in any competitive devaluation, Chief Secretary for Administration Chan said. [*R/HK] \par \par \uc2  -- Taiwan Premier Siew said the government's top priority is to stabilize the capital markets, according the Economic Daily News. He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy is to respect market forces and provide adequate liquidity to the market. The New Taiwan dollar closed at a new 11-year low on continued yen weakness. [*R/TW] \par \par \uc2  -- Taiwan's stock index fell 1.8% on the New Taiwan dollar's weakness and weak May sales reports. [*R/TW] \par \par \uc2  -- Moody's has placed the ratings of four Japanese real estate companies - Mitsubishi Estate, Mitsui Fudosan, Sumitomo Realty & Development and Tokyo Tatemono - on review for possible downgrade, citing heightened cost structures, declines in property prices and limited recovery of office rents. [*R/JA] \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par               Stock Index                       \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par                          Change      Level     Tuesday  Monday\par Hong Kong  Hang Seng     Dn 195.17  8391.46   HK$7.7485 HK$7.7487\par Indonesisa Jakarta Comp  Up 1.653   411.072  IDR11,812 IDR11,750\par Japan      Nikkei        Up 235.46 15,530.17  Y140.13  Y140.66\par S. Korea   Kospi         Dn  6.66   339.22   KRW1,395 KRW1,399\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 09-06-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1156GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1042 4190 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6904xaa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
