\par\par \b \uc2  NZ Dlr/Early Trade -2: Watching A$ For More  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 324 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 1998\par 00:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The other big factor influencing the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar Friday is the Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been subject to series of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past 15 hours. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, Reserve Bank of Australia Governor Ian MacFarlane confirmed the Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Thursday to support the Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Overnight, New York traders told Dow Jones Newswires that the New York Federal Reserve bought Australian dollars on behalf of the Reserve Bank of Australia, at around 0940 GMT when they were at US$0.6155. At that point, both the New York Federal Reserve Bank and the New York office of the Reserve Bank of Australia declined to comment. \par \par \uc2  And Sydney \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said the Reserve Bank of Australia has again bought Australian dollars Friday morning, at US$0.6090. \par \par \uc2  But New Zealand traders said Friday that U.S. funds have still been selling aggressively, as have sellers out of Japan. \par \par \uc2  Prior to the Moody's statement, traders said the New Zealand dollar had held up quite well in the face of the Australian weakness, although one trader described that as puzzling. They said there was a risk the selling undermining the Australian dollar could spread to the New Zealand \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Against its trade weighted index, the New Zealand dollar has fallen to 51.96 from 58.35 late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank's Monetary Conditions Index is at 241, 109 basis points below the 350 level the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it desired for the third quarter. \par \par \uc2  On a cross rate with the neighboring Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the local dollar fell to A$0.8528 from A$0.8574 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On a cross rate with the Japanese yen, the local dollar fell to Y71.97\par from Y72.48 late Thursday.\par -By Karen Chan; 644-801-8960; email kchan@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 04-06-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2218GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1062 20711 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6404t3r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
