\par\par \b \uc2  NZ Dlr Up In Early Trading; Supported By Australian Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 393 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 1998\par 22:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones Australia and New Zealand Report \par \uc2 DJAN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--The New Zealand dollar is higher in local morning trade Tuesday, with dealers saying the unit has moved up on the back of gains in the Australian dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Australian dollar is being supported by Reserve Bank of Australia buying of that unit. \par \par \uc2  Around 2045 GMT the New Zealand dollar was quoted at US$0.5339, up from US$0.5329 late Monday in Wellington. \par \par \uc2  The New Zealand \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a range of US$0.5310 to US$0.5330 overnight. \par \par \uc2  One dealer said the local unit has moved up on gains in the Australian dollar with market talk that the Australian unit is being bought by the Reserve Bank of Australia. \par \par \uc2  "The New Zealand dollar has moved up a little bit with the Australian unit coming up with talk of Australian Reserve Bank buying the aussie," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said he had also heard talk of Australian Reserve Bank buying the Australian unit. \par \par \uc2  "The Australian unit was down and now has jumped up and it seems that the Reserve Bank has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the brokers," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar will likely move in a range of US$0.5325 to US$0.5350 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "The movement of the kiwi will just depend on the aussie movements - if they're a bit more exaggerated the New Zealand dollar could perhaps bust out of that range," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Against its trade weighted index, the New Zealand dollar rose to 58.74 from 58.69 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Around 2045 GMT the Reserve Bank's Monetary Conditions Index, which is a composite measure of the trade-weighted index measure of the NZ dollar and yields on 90-day bank bills, is at 329, or 171 basis points below the 500 level the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on March 18 outlined as appropriate on average during the second quarter of 1998. \par \par \uc2  On a cross rate with the neighboring Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the local dollar fell to A$0.8528 from A$0.8558 late Monday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On a cross rate with the Japanese yen, the local dollar rose to Y72.75\par from Y71.95 late Monday.\par    -By Alan Wood; 644-801-8960 awood@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 18-05-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2056GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1062 20711 \par \par \uc2 Dokument djan000020010916du5i002u8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
