\par\par \b \uc2  NZ Dollar Up In Late Trading; Tracks Australian Dollar \b0\par\par\uc2 395 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 1998\par 05:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--The New Zealand dollar is higher in local afternoon trade Friday, with dealers saying trading has been volatile, mainly tracking the Australian dollar during the session. \par \par \uc2  The local dollar bounced sharply higher at around 2248 GMT, after the Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied on the back of rumors the Reserve Bank of Australia was buying the Australian dollar earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  From a low of US$0.5629 before 2248 GMT, the New Zealand dollar reached a peak of US$0.5719 before losing a little ground. \par \par \uc2  One broker noted the U.S. dollar lost ground versus the yen at about 2248 GMT. \par \par \uc2  'It sparked a bit of rumor, because the dollar/yen dropped below Y132.00 around the same time, as to whether there had been some coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  going on,' he said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0400 GMT the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is quoted at US$0.5706, up from US$0.5686 late Thursday in Wellington, and higher from its local open at US$0.5657. \par \par \uc2  One trader said the local dollar closed near the upper end of its range Friday, however noting little change in the composite trade weighted index TWI and the monetary conditions index MCI. \par \par \uc2  Against the TWI the New Zealand dollar (NZ$) is NZ$61.85, just higher from NZ$61.82 late Thursday and slightly lower from NZ$61.86 early Friday. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank's MCI, which is a composite measure of the trade-weighted index measure of the NZ dollar and yields on 90-day bank bills, is late Friday at 607, or 43 basis points below the 650 level the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Dec. 16 outlined as appropriate on average during the first quarter of 1998. \par \par \uc2  On a cross-rate with the neighboring Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the local dollar is quoted at A$0.8923, down from A$0.8947 late Thursday and from A$0.8937 early Friday. \par \par \uc2  On a cross-rate with the Japanese yen, the local dollar was quoted at Y75.23, up from Y75.14 late Thursday and steady from Y75.23 early Friday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the New Zealand dollar will likely move in a range of US$0.5670 to US$0.5730 overnight. \par \par \uc2  -By Alan Wood; 644-801-8960 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 09-01-98 \par \par \uc2  0417GMT \par \par \uc2  1062 20711 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du19006ok\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
