\par\par \b \uc2  NZ Reserve Bank Says It Doesn't  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Mkts \b0\par\par\uc2 246 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 1998\par 03:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday said it doesn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  'The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets,' Reserve Bank Communications Manager Paul Jackman told Dow Jones. \par \par \uc2  The New Zealand dollar rose against the U.S. dollar in afternoon trading Friday, after the Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied on the back of rumors of Australian Reserve Bank buying of the Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  Around 0220 GMT the New Zealand dollar was quoted at US$0.5686, up from a intraday low of US$0.5630 seen earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of Australia was in the market checking Australian dollar levels in mid-morning Australian trading, according to Australian dealers. The Australian dollar rallied sharply on the talk of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  checking levels of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders in Australia said that they believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  actually bought Australian dollars in large amounts in exchange for U.S. dollars. \par \par \uc2  An Australian trader earlier Friday said he had been contacted by the Reserve Bank and added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought Australian dollars at US$0.6320, near its intraday low Friday. \par \par \uc2  At 0220 GMT, the Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at US$0.6370, up from an earlier low of US$0.6315. \par \par \uc2  -By Chris Ritchie;644-8018960 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 09-01-98 \par \par \uc2  0235GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du19006h9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
