\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  in NZ dollar won't work, say analysts. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Simon Louisson \par \uc2 750 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WELLINGTON, Dec 9 (Reuter) - New Zealand \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts on Monday dismissed as counter-productive apparent hints by Labour Party finance spokesman Michael Cullen that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  Cullen, who is Labour's candidate for finance minister if it clinches a coalition with the New Zealand First party, caused a mild stir in financial markets last week when he sent a coded message about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  First is expected to decide on Tuesday whether it will support Labour or the conservative National Party. \par \par \uc2  In his speech, Cullen said there were various "highly orthodox and commonly practised ways" of addressing the exchange rate, which he has consistently described as overvalued. \par \par \uc2  He declined to go into detail, but said calls for dropping interest rates missed the point and the exchange rate itself was the primary problem. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  experts all took Cullen to mean that the Reserve Bank should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly to bring the dollar down, something never done since the kiwi was floated in March 1985. \par \par \uc2  The kiwi, which recently touched 8-1/2 year highs, is one of the freest floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world but RBNZ Governor Don Brash reserves the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Brash last week told Reuters he did not wish to air his views on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In the past he has pointed to the failure of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by other countries, notably Britain in 1992. \par \par \uc2  "It doesn't work very well and can be counter-productive under certain circumstances. The general view on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is that it is not particularly effective," said Bankers Trust economist David Plank. \par \par \uc2  "The very short term impact (of RBNZ selling) might be for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to dip, but the general experience around the world is (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is) very ineffective but good at wasting taxpayers' money." \par \par \uc2  Cullen has argued that part of the reason for the kiwi's steep climb -- up 25 percent on a Trade-Weighted Index basis in three years -- is that investing in the New Zealand dollar is a one-way bet, and he wants to dispel that notion. \par \par \uc2  Brash caused a stir in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market last week when he said that the New Zealand dollar appeared to be near the top of its cycle. Plank believes the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is 10-15 percent overvalued. \par \par \uc2  But not everyone agrees. \par \par \uc2  National Bank chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer Stu Nattrass said the exchange rate had only recovered to the level it was at in 1988, after which the country went into deep recession. \par \par \uc2  He said inflation expectations are the seat of the problem and the reason why wholesale interest rates are at 8.5 percent while inflation is expected to be at one percent in 1997. \par \par \uc2  "Interest rates are far more relevant than exchange rates. I'm surprised people are focusing on the exchange rate and not interest rates as being way out of line," Nattrass said. \par \par \uc2  A dealer who did not wish to be named said that if the RBNZ directly sells New Zealand dollars it will simply provide cheap rates for investors to buy the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "You would quickly find a level of willing buyers," he said. \par \par \uc2  One bank's chief bond dealer said any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would indicate the RB's autonomy had been undermined. \par \par \uc2  "It would not be the amount the bank sold, just that they are sellers. I would see that as being bearish, showing political influence coming back into the Reserve Bank and therefore they are losing their independence," he said. \par \par \uc2  Under the Reserve Bank Act, the finance minister can request an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but the governor is as liberty to ignore it if such a move would threaten the bank's goal of achieving price stability. The government can demand action but needs to get an Order in Council, a move requiring cabinet approval and signature by the governor-general. \par \par \uc2  Even exporters doubt \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would work. \par \par \uc2  Malcolm Bailey, president of lobby group Federated Farmers and spokesman for an exporters' crisis summit on the exchange rate last week, said: "I don't think selling New Zealand dollars will be the answer." \par \par \uc2  He said exporters are not looking for quick fix solutions, although he agreed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could "burst the bubble of over-enthusiasm about investing in New Zealand". \par \par \uc2  "If you have the government behind the Reserve Bank pulling the levers, then you undermine confidence in the Reserve Bank Act," he said. -- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019dsc902hcx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
