\par\par \b \uc2  NZ Labour's Cullen/NZ Dlr -2: In Coalition Talks \b0\par\par\uc2 251 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 1996\par 00:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Cullen's Labour Party and the National party are separately negotiating with New Zealand First to form the next government. Labour leader Helen Clark recently reiterated that Cullen would be minister of finance in a Labour-led government. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in New Zealand is independent, but many major decisions are conducted through consultation with the minister of finance, analysts note. \par \par \uc2  Cullen said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should signal 'it's prepared to operate directly, without specifying the means it might use' in an effort to fight the impression by international investors that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a one-way bet. \par \par \uc2  A spokeswoman for Cullen said the comment was intentionally vague and didn't imply an immediate call for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was floated in March 1985. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would sell \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars and likely buy U.S. Treasurys if it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it would soak up the excess liquidity created by issuing government-backed Treasury bills. \par \par \uc2  The government would in effect underwrite the issuance of Treasury bills the Reserve Bank would need to issue to soak up liquidity after selling the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Reserve Bank now issues Treasury bills in weekly tenders and also in open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But the amount would increase dramatically in an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and interest rates on the Treasury bills would likely rise as a result. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 25-11-96 \par \par \uc2  2300GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011014dsbp018bc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
