\par\par \b \uc2  NZ/Dollar/ \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -2: Australia  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Noted \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 1996\par 23:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  But talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gained some ground as international investors look at the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of other central banks. \par \par \uc2  Traders note the Reserve Bank of Australia has been active in the market, and overseas investors have begun to speculate the Reserve Bank of New Zealand may mimic its neighbor. \par \par \uc2  In a December 1993 article in the Reserve Bank of Australia bulletin, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  defended its decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  'We have been less inclined than most other countries to direct monetary policy at the exchange rate, but have used \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  quite often,' the Reserve Bank of Australia said. 'We see no need to be defensive about the use of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as it has probably had a stabilizing influence and been moderately profitable.' \par \par \uc2  Although the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an independent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , any decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market would likely come in consultation with the Minister of Finance, analysts say. \par \par \uc2  That's because the government would in effect underwrite the issuance of Treasury bills the Reserve Bank would need to issue to soak up liquidity after selling the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Reserve Bank now issues Treasury bills in weekly tenders and also in open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But the amount would increase dramatically in an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and interest rates on the Treasury bills would likely rise as a result. \par \par \uc2  The weighted-average yield on NZ$75 million of three-month T-bills rose to 9.05% from 8.824% in the most recent tender. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank could also issue Reserve Bank bills which is what the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses for daily liquidity management. But analysts say that would be highly unlikely. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 13-11-96 \par \par \uc2  2202GMT \par \par \uc2  1199 20713 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011014dsbd00vaa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
