\par\par \b \uc2  NZ's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  -4: Brash Qualifies Statements On Policy \b0\par\par\uc2 443 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juni 1995\par 00:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is required under the Reserve Bank Act to keep underlying inflation (the CPI minus one-time price spikes and interest rates) below 2.0% annually. \par \par \uc2  Its failure to keep underlying inflation within that target range could be grounds for New Zealand Minister of Finance Bill Birch to request an explanation and possibly replace Reserve Bank Governor Don Brash for failing to hit the target. \par \par \uc2  Brash actually signed a contract with the government, the Policy Target Agreement in 1992, promising to keep underlying inflation within the 0% to 2% range. \par \par \uc2  It is unlikely that Birch will take such an extreme measure as replacing Brash. But he did confirm Wednesday he would ask the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's non-executive directors to submit a report on the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  of monetary policy should the underlying rate exceed the 2.0% range as forecast. \par \par \uc2  At a press conference before the release of the MPS, Brash said he had spoken to Birch Wednesday and that he doesn't plan on resigning from his post and wasn't asked to do so. \par \par \uc2  Brash said in his statement to the market that 'monetary conditions must remain firm.' \par \par \uc2  But he qualified the timing of how long short-term interest rates would remain above the current 9.0% level. Most mortgages in New Zealand are borrowed at a rate about 2.0 percentage points above the 90-day bank bill rate. Current rates are about 11.0%. The MPS says 'the 90-day bank bill rate is assumed to remain over 9.0% for at least the rest of 1995, before declining gradually.' \par \par \uc2  'As additional information is received, it may become apparent that an earlier easing of monetary conditions is warranted,' Brash said. 'Conversely, if indicators point to stronger momentum behind inflation than we currently estimate, not only would easing in monetary conditions be delayed, but a further firming would be required. Either way, the Reserve Bank will take whatever action is necessary to maintain price stability.' \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, but uses about $20 million (\b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) to facilitate inter-bank daily cash settlements. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can send the 90-day bank bill rate higher by withdrawing some or all of its daily settlement cash. The markets have moved in recent months to take the 90-day bank bill rates near the 9.0% level. \par \par \uc2  Brash said at a press conference before the release of the MPS that 'if monetary conditions were to ease,' a change in the cash target would be 'entirely possible.' \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 28-06-95 \par \par \uc2  2216GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr6s04upk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
