\par\par \b \uc2  NZ/Brash -4: Kiwi On TWI Basis Below Mid-'84 Level \b0\par\par\uc2 365 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 1995\par 04:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Co., Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to influence the value of the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does monitor closely the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trade-weighted value, and through its comments and adjustments to money market liquidity levels it can affect the value of the New Zealand dollar on a trade-weighted basis. \par \par \uc2  The most recent comment by the Reserve Bank on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  occured in February, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  indicated it was concerned with a decline in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trade-weighted value. At that time the New Zealand dollar had dropped to 59.16 against its trade-weighted index. \par \par \uc2  The trade weighted index (TWI) is a weighted basket measuring the New Zealand dollar against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of five major trading partners. The index currently is around 59.47. During 1994 it ranged between 55.24 and 60.28. \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank closely monitors the New Zealand dollar's trade-weighted value because the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  influences the nation's inflation rate through prices paid for imports. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legally mandated to keep the underlying inflation rate at 0%-2%. \par \par \uc2  In his speech to the farmers' group, Brash reaffirmed a Reserve Bank forecast for the appreciation of the New Zealand dollar's trade-weighted value. 'Our most recent projection for inflation is based on annual appreciation in the TWI of about 2%, and this appears at this stage to be consistent with underlying inflation moving gradually back towards the center of our 0% to 2% target,' he said. \par \par \uc2  Brash also noted that the current level of the trade-weighted index still is below the level reached after a major devaluation in mid-1984. \par \par \uc2  'It is relevant to note that between the beginning of 1991 and the beginning of 1995, the TWI appreciated by a total of little more than 3%, considerably less than an average of 2% annually. Indeed, at this stage the Kiwi (New Zealand) dollar on a TWI basis remains below its level immediately after the July 1984 devaluation,' he said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-04-95 \par \par \uc2  0258GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011025dr4a02ir4\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (new zealand near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\b